Done. Issue 18 complete, committed as `d85baf3`, state marker set to `done`.

**What landed:**
- **`GET /api/log?ticket=<id>&attempt=<n>&offset=<bytes>`** — serves an attempt's raw log from a byte offset, ANSI-stripped server-side, reporting `offset`/`nextOffset`/`totalSize` plus the ticket's attempt list (implement/resolver/reconstructed, with rotated `attempt-N` files resolvable). Chunks at 64KB with UTF-8-safe boundaries; the offset contract is what ticket 19's tailing reuses.
- **Events endpoint** now also returns the ticket's `spec` text (issue body after the title), feeding the never-run fallback.
- **UI**: Detail renders the raw log pane below the timeline; clicking an attempt row switches the pane to that attempt's log; a never-run ticket shows its spec text with a "no attempts yet" marker instead of timeline and log. Selection and the never-run fallback are pure projection; fetched content/selection live in module scope so full-DOM rebuilds never drop them.

**Verification:** 177 engine/server/fleet + 68 UI tests pass, both `tsc --noEmit`, `vite build` clean. A review pass (code-review skill) flagged UTF-8 chunk-splitting and duplicated state reset — both fixed and pinned by tests. Tail-first loading and snapshot-refetch liveness are deferred to ticket 19 by design.
